Jenkins Plugins:
Pipeline Plugin - For creating and managing CI/CD pipelines.
Git Plugin - For version control integration with Git repositories.
SonarQube Scanner for Jenkins - For integrating SonarQube code quality analysis.
Nexus Platform Plugin - For interacting with Nexus repositories (artifact management).
Docker Pipeline - To build and deploy Docker images.
Kubernetes Plugin - For deploying applications to Kubernetes clusters.
Blue Ocean - For a modern UI and visualization of Jenkins pipelines.
Email Extension Plugin - For sending email notifications on build status.
Slack Notification Plugin - For sending notifications to Slack.
Workspace Cleanup Plugin - To clean up the workspace before builds.
OWASP Dependency-Check Plugin - To identify project dependencies and report known vulnerabilities.
OWASP ZAP Plugin - To integrate automated security testing into the pipeline.
Additional Tools:
SonarQube - For static code analysis and quality checks.
Nexus Repository Manager - For managing artifacts and dependencies.
Docker - For containerization of applications.
Kubernetes - For orchestration and management of containerized applications.
Git - For version control.
Maven/Gradle - For build automation (if applicable).
Jenkinsfile - For defining the pipeline in a declarative manner.
OWASP ZAP - An open-source security scanner for finding vulnerabilities in web applications.
OWASP Dependency-Check - A tool that identifies project dependencies and checks them against known vulnerabilities.
Integrating OWASP tools into the Jenkins pipeline helps ensure that security is considered throughout the development lifecycle, promoting safer application deployments.

